# The REPOSITORY ITSELF. `assets.directory` is "." — the whole folder — so
# without this line wrangler uploads .git/ as public files, and it did: the
# 2026-08-20 deploy served /.git/config, /.git/HEAD and every loose object at
# sketchcast.app, which is enough to clone the full history off the marketing
# site. Nothing secret was exposed (this repo holds no secrets by design and the
# GitHub mirror is public), but it is 700-odd files of pure surface, and the day
# a secret does land in history this would publish it.
.git

# Tooling state that lives in this folder and is not the site. Same reason as
# .git: assets.directory is "." so anything here ships unless named. Both were
# caught SERVING on 2026-08-22 — /.wrangler/tmp/…/no-op-worker.js.map and
# /.pytest_cache/CACHEDIR.TAG both returned 200 from sketchcast.app. Neither is
# secret; both are pure surface, and .wrangler is where wrangler keeps local
# state, which is not a directory to publish on principle.
.wrangler
.pytest_cache

wrangler.jsonc
.gitignore
.assetsignore
README*
.env*

# Build-time only — the generator, its inputs and its tooling never ship.
# (Its OUTPUT — the <locale>/ folders, sitemap.xml, robots.txt — does.)
build-i18n.mjs
strings
package.json
package-lock.json
node_modules
